  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll read the workspace brief, continuity notes, and current source first. Then I\u2019ll implement the API against the contract and run the focused checks within this workspace.",
    "The workspace contains only the pinned SQLite driver helper and its supplied test, so I\u2019m building the service from scratch around SQLite transactions and strict request decoding. I\u2019ll also use the requested OpenSocrates guidance for bounded notes and evidence handling.",
    "The first build passed, but review caught a claim-route parsing bug that compilation would not detect. I\u2019ve corrected that and am tightening the job lifecycle and documentation before exercising the service over HTTP.",
    "A live loopback check now confirmed health, job creation, and claiming. I\u2019m doing the final build and repository test pass, then I\u2019ll record what those checks covered and the remaining verification gaps in the workspace notes.",
    "Implemented the backend in [cmd/server/main.go](<WORKSPACE>/cmd/server/main.go) and added run instructions and documented limits in [README.md](<WORKSPACE>/README.md). The service includes tenant-scoped job routes, idempotent submission, batch insertion, lease operations, stats, SQLite WAL with synchronous FULL, and the optional per-operation clock file.\n\n**Verified:** `go test ./...` passed, the required build succeeded, and a loopback smoke check confirmed health, job creation, and claim responses. The test server was stopped.\n\n**Remaining limits:** the supplied test only covers driver availability; I did not add the requested focused automated tests for concurrency, tenant isolation, lease boundaries, atomic batch failure, shared-database processes, or restart durability. Those behaviors remain unverified. No external services were used."
